{{~##
   The opening markup every generated page shares: the stylesheet, the icon sheet, the
   top bar with the theme control, the breadcrumb, and the sibling list down the side.

   Nothing here is fetched. The stylesheet is inline rather than beside the pages, and
   the icons and the brand mark with it, because the tool is expected to run on closed
   networks - which the history page two directories away states as its reason for
   reaching no CDN at all. It used to be Bootstrap 4.3.1 from a CDN that has since shut
   down, so the pages had been rendering unstyled and a golden comparison could not tell:
   it checks that the markup has not changed, not that a url still answers.

   Do not write a Scriban delimiter inside one of these comment blocks, not even inside
   a backtick. The closing brace pair ends the block wherever it appears, and the rest
   of the comment is then page text - which is what this footer did, in every page of
   every project, until it was noticed by eye.

   The colours are tokens, defined three times over: the light set on the root, the dark
   set behind a media query for a reader who has chosen no theme here, and the dark set
   again behind an attribute for a reader who has. The last one is what makes the control
   in the bar able to override the operating system in both directions. A small script in
   the head applies the stored choice before the first paint, because applying it after
   is a flash of the other theme on every page.

   The icons are one symbol sheet per page and one `use` per place, rather than the
   markup repeated: a side list names every table, so a project with 500 of them would
   otherwise carry 500 copies of the same path. Line art rather than emoji - emoji are a
   font's opinion and differ per platform.

   The brand mark is the 32px icon, drawn at 18. brand/build-assets.mjs makes both it and
   the favicon; the favicon is the 16px one, and stays separate because a page's tab icon
   and its bar are different sizes.
##~}}
